## Why This Is Asked
Tests tenant isolation across storage, compute, and code execution, with concrete tools and trade-offs.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant isolation and data encryption at rest/in use
- Hardware-backed KMS and CMK management
- Micro-segmentation and per-tenant namespaces
- Runtime attestation for UDFs/WASM
- SBOM provenance and auditability
- Incident response and key management

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: rotate a tenant's envelope key and re-encrypt data
async function rotateTenantKey(tenantId){
  const cmk = await kms.getTenantCMK(tenantId);
  const dataKey = await kms.generateDataKey(cmk);
  await storage.reencryptTenantData(tenantId, dataKey);
  await audit.log(`Rotated key for ${tenantId}`);
}
```

